WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
(dramatic orchestral music)

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.640
- First of all I want to say thank you.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.980
Everyone's a fan, a serious fan.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.300
I'm keeping my cool right
now, even when you walked in,

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.174
but we're all super big fans here,

00:00:11.174 --> 00:00:13.580
and I'm gonna be chill about it.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.690
But I wanted to do
something sweet for you,

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:18.490
so we made it a little afternoon
delight, a spot of tea,

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:20.050
because of how the Brits do.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.764
So, feel free, pour.

00:00:21.764 --> 00:00:23.240
(orchestral music)

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.218
- Nicely brewed.
- Nicely brewed.

00:00:24.218 --> 00:00:25.051
- Is that coffee?
- So we did all right?

00:00:25.051 --> 00:00:25.884
- This is tea.

00:00:25.884 --> 00:00:27.283
- This is tea it's all tea.
- In a coffee pot?

00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:28.560
- Earl grey.
- [Hugh] In a coffee pot.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.515
- We thought we'd throw
you off a little bit, Hugh.

00:00:31.515 --> 00:00:32.348
(laughing)
- What makes that possible-

00:00:32.348 --> 00:00:33.700
- Hugh is all of a sudden my favorite.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.680
- I think traditionally the coffee pot

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.265
is the slightly taller one.

00:00:37.265 --> 00:00:38.290
- Oh, it is.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.560
- The belly of this
allows the tea to brew,

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.910
the leaves to brew you see.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.070
- To get a full bodied--

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:43.903
- Yeah.

00:00:43.903 --> 00:00:44.736
- aroma.
- That's my theory anyway.

00:00:44.736 --> 00:00:45.569
- I love it.

00:00:45.569 --> 00:00:46.500
I love it, we're learning.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.856
Oh, can I have some of that?

00:00:47.856 --> 00:00:48.689
- Of course.
- All right.

00:00:48.689 --> 00:00:49.630
(orchestral music)

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.210
I didn't bring you here
just to sip some tea,

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:54.291
I wanted to spill some tea,
so I thought of a game.

00:00:54.291 --> 00:00:56.220
I like to call it sip it and spill it,

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.400
and it's basically a very
sophisticated version

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.920
of Never Have I Ever, so I'm trying

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.180
to keep something very
American and trashy, classy.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:03.013
(crowd laughing)

00:01:03.013 --> 00:01:04.730
But, for example, sip it and spill it

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.130
if you ever locked yourself in a bathroom

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.700
with a glass of wine
because you have children

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.170
and you just want a minute to yourself.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.310
See then I would take this bad boy,

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:13.540
and I'd drink the whole thing.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.794
- I'd have to drink that
with you, I'm afraid.

00:01:14.794 --> 00:01:16.032
(laughing)

00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:16.950
- I'm like, I just need--
- Sorry.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.822
- Mommy needs a minute.
- Yeah.

00:01:18.822 --> 00:01:19.655
(laughing)

00:01:19.655 --> 00:01:20.970
- Okay, I have one.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.990
Sip it and spill it if you've
ever rolled Easter eggs

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:26.577
while wearing a bonnet and dress.

00:01:26.577 --> 00:01:28.994
(jazz music)

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.334
- It's you?

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:33.330
- [Michelle] It's Hugh.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:34.534
- You wear a bonnet often?

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:35.770
(plates clattering)

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:36.667
Oh my God.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:37.500
- But you know, it was Easter.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.470
My friends said, "Put on a dress,

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.810
and let's roll the Easter egg
down the hills", so you know.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:43.268
- This makes you my favorite
person at the table once again.

00:01:43.268 --> 00:01:44.101
(laughing)
- You said that twice.

00:01:44.101 --> 00:01:45.650
- I know, once again.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:47.180
Okay wait, Hugh your turn.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:50.170
- Sip it and spill it if
you've ever snogged Brad Pitt.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:51.650
- Snogged means kissed right?

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:52.483
- Yes, kiss.

00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:53.316
- Are you about to sip your tea?

00:01:53.316 --> 00:01:54.149
- Shall I show you?

00:01:54.149 --> 00:01:54.982
Well I'm just bit, you know just--

00:01:54.982 --> 00:01:56.605
(coughing)

00:01:56.605 --> 00:01:57.438
- Go Elizabeth.

00:01:57.438 --> 00:01:58.479
- What's that story?

00:01:58.479 --> 00:01:59.670
(crowd applauding)

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:00.890
- Somebody had to.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.270
- Somebody had to sacrifice.

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:06.600
- I did it as a paid job
because we were on a set,

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.900
- What a beautifully paid job.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.000
- acting in a part, yes, indeed.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.954
There are worst ways to earn a living.

00:02:10.954 --> 00:02:11.787
- Wow.

00:02:11.787 --> 00:02:12.620
- So I was not complaining, but yeah.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.673
He cut his teeth with me I think, yeah.

00:02:14.673 --> 00:02:15.506
(crowd clapping)

00:02:15.506 --> 00:02:16.339
- Nice
- As it were.

00:02:16.339 --> 00:02:17.594
- Did you teach him how to snog as well?

00:02:17.594 --> 00:02:18.427
- I made him, I made
him the man that he is.

00:02:18.427 --> 00:02:19.900
- You made him a good snogger?

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.310
- Yes, he's learned everything--

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:22.710
- I always love that y'all call it that

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:24.579
because it sounds not cool.

00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:25.412
(laughing)

00:02:25.412 --> 00:02:26.245
- Yeah.

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:27.078
- Okay, your turn Allen.

00:02:27.078 --> 00:02:29.220
- Sip it and spill it if you've ever put

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:33.170
on a Downton costume, or
any costume, backwards.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.003
- Oh.

00:02:34.003 --> 00:02:34.836
- You did, wait what?

00:02:34.836 --> 00:02:35.680
What do you mean backwards?

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:36.513
How did you do that?

00:02:36.513 --> 00:02:38.380
- It used to happen a lot
because sometimes the costumes

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:40.250
are the same on the front
as they are on the back

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.819
so there'll be like an
embellishment on the front

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:45.100
and you know a slightly
maybe varied pattern

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.930
on the back, but you can't
really tell the difference

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:49.300
so it happened a few times.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.950
- How far did you go with it I mean--

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:52.285
- I actually turned up on set--

00:02:52.285 --> 00:02:53.118
- Is it on camera?

00:02:53.118 --> 00:02:55.540
- and went the neck feels really high

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.069
and the back's a little low.

00:02:57.069 --> 00:02:59.693
(laughing)

00:02:59.693 --> 00:03:00.526
So yes, I have.

00:03:00.526 --> 00:03:04.810
- Sip it and spill it, if after
a night of wild carousing,

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.360
you ended up sleeping in your trailer

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:09.940
on the set of Downton Abbey.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:11.586
(laughing)

00:03:11.586 --> 00:03:12.419
Huh?

00:03:12.419 --> 00:03:15.235
- Oh gosh!

00:03:15.235 --> 00:03:16.068
- It's a true story.

00:03:16.068 --> 00:03:18.070
- I remember this night so well.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.620
- Maybe you know it's a long day.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.360
It was during summer where
we have a light refreshment.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.750
So we got very very refreshed

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.380
on hard cider called Old Rosie.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:29.850
She's a cruel mistress because--

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:30.850
- She sounds fun.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:31.683
- Oh, she was fun.

00:03:31.683 --> 00:03:32.516
But she's great.

00:03:32.516 --> 00:03:34.190
So I had the great idea, "I'll
just go back to the castle,

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:37.400
I'll sleep in the castle",
or like, in my trailer.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.900
And then so basically
I'll be ready for work.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.483
I'll just roll out of the
trailer but the problem is,

00:03:40.483 --> 00:03:44.090
there's a 15 foot gate outside
of the castle so I was like,

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.650
"Uh it's gonna take all
of my MacGyver skills".

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:47.483
- You scaled the gate?

00:03:47.483 --> 00:03:48.316
- I did.

00:03:48.316 --> 00:03:50.155
It wasn't the greatest idea I've ever had.

00:03:50.155 --> 00:03:50.988
(laughing)

00:03:50.988 --> 00:03:51.821
Eh, I'm gonna be honest I was like--

00:03:51.821 --> 00:03:53.072
- Can I say something else?

00:03:53.072 --> 00:03:53.905
- Yeah.

00:03:53.905 --> 00:03:55.440
- It's pitch black like you can't even--

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.273
- Yeah.

00:03:56.273 --> 00:03:57.106
- begin to describe--

00:03:57.106 --> 00:03:57.939
- It's out in the countryside--

00:03:57.939 --> 00:03:58.772
there's no
- because there's no light.

00:03:58.772 --> 00:03:59.605
- Yeah yeah.

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:02.220
- I once tried, I drove
myself one day to the set.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.220
All I had to do was drive to the gate.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.960
I couldn't even find the gate.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.090
- Did the car not have headlights?

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:11.547
- Yeah it had headlights but
they went like about two feet

00:04:11.547 --> 00:04:13.019
and then it was black.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.008
- The weak headlights.

00:04:14.008 --> 00:04:15.314
(wheezing)

00:04:15.314 --> 00:04:17.024
[Michele] And I didn't
understand because she said--

00:04:17.024 --> 00:04:17.857
- And I was, I actually was in a ditch

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.430
and the wheels were
spinning and I couldn't get,

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:20.957
I couldn't actually get out of it.

00:04:20.957 --> 00:04:22.182
(laughing)
(laughter drowns out sounds)

00:04:22.182 --> 00:04:24.470
- And I was like--

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:26.269
(fake sobbing)

00:04:26.269 --> 00:04:27.102
I'm not kidding.

00:04:27.102 --> 00:04:27.935
- Oooh.

00:04:27.935 --> 00:04:28.768
(laughing)

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:30.240
- Uh, sip it and spill it
if you've ever fallen out

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.343
of your tiny pair of speedo
swimming trunks while on set.

00:04:35.724 --> 00:04:38.360
(laughing)
(mumbling)

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:39.350
(crowd laughing)

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:40.860
Why were you wearing speedos on set?

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:43.930
- It wasn't on Downton set, it
was on one of my first jobs.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.267
The people who were doing
the costume wrote and said,

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:48.040
"Oh uh, a young boy and his father".

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.180
I was 17.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.710
So when I arrived, all
of the speedos were like

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:53.107
for eight or nine year olds.

00:04:53.107 --> 00:04:53.940
(laughing)

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.730
So then, and they were like,
"We don't have time just,

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.130
we're gonna have to, you
know, just, you're gonna

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.400
have to try and fit into one of them."

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:02.280
And then in one take they went,
"And okay just hold there".

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.113
And I said, "What", and
I was kind of agitated.

00:05:03.113 --> 00:05:04.220
"What, what was the problem?"

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.975
They were like, "Your just, your um..."

00:05:05.975 --> 00:05:08.279
(laughs loudly)

00:05:08.279 --> 00:05:09.353
- It came out?

00:05:09.353 --> 00:05:10.186
(laughing)

00:05:10.186 --> 00:05:12.291
That is like...oh my gosh.

00:05:12.291 --> 00:05:13.124
That's...horrifying.

00:05:13.124 --> 00:05:14.752
- It was pretty embarrassing, yeah yep.

00:05:14.752 --> 00:05:15.627
- Oh but kind of funny.

00:05:15.627 --> 00:05:17.111
- That's why I can't
even look at a speedo.

00:05:17.111 --> 00:05:17.944
(laughing)

00:05:17.944 --> 00:05:18.956
- By the way, grapes?

00:05:18.956 --> 00:05:21.320
(laughing)

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:22.420
- Fig?

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:23.570
- Thank you.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:24.690
- Wait, what is that because

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:25.750
I actually don't know what that is.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:26.626
- It's a fig.

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:27.459
- Fig.

00:05:27.459 --> 00:05:28.292
- Do you just eat it like that?

00:05:28.292 --> 00:05:30.060
I've only seen it as like
a spread or some sort.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.440
- It's a real technique, I'll show you.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:32.842
- Okay, it's a real technique?

00:05:32.842 --> 00:05:35.060
(laughing)

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.410
Hugh, you're awesome.

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:38.510
All right, sip it and
spill it if you've had

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:40.749
the greatest time ever
at the most amazing--

00:05:40.749 --> 00:05:41.670
(cheering)
(cheering drowns out sounds)

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:42.590
- Exactly, Hugh.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:44.162
- [Hugh] You never do that.

00:05:44.162 --> 00:05:45.459
You would never do that.

00:05:45.459 --> 00:05:47.230
- Oh well you do in America, Hugh.

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.709
- Oh sip it and stuff it, Hugh.

00:05:48.709 --> 00:05:49.827
- Sip it and stuff it.

00:05:49.827 --> 00:05:50.660
(laughing)

